sfx2: a LOK kernel registers no DDE service

On Windows SfxApplication::InitializeDde registers two DDE services in
every process, LOK or not. Under LOK Application::GetAppName() is
empty, so the first answers any service name (DNS_FILTEROFF): any
program in the same session could have the kernel open a document by
path (ImplDdeService::MakeTopic) or run a System topic command, past
the client's own checks, and a DDE link to a server that is not there
connected to another LOK process instead.
With LibreOfficeKit active no service is registered. The callers
already take a missing service: AddDdeTopic returns, RemoveDdeTopic
finds no topics, the document shells test GetDdeService(). DDE links
out of a document, the client side, are untouched.

--- a/sfx2/source/appl/appdde.cxx
+++ b/sfx2/source/appl/appdde.cxx
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
 #include <tools/debug.hxx>
 #include <tools/urlobj.hxx>
 #include <comphelper/diagnose_ex.hxx>
+#include <comphelper/lok.hxx>
 #include <unotools/pathoptions.hxx>
 #include <vcl/svapp.hxx>
 
@@ -407,6 +408,9 @@
 {
     int nError = 0;
 #if defined(_WIN32)
+    // Ely: a LOK client's kernel serves no DDE.
+    if (comphelper::LibreOfficeKit::isActive())
+        return true;
     DBG_ASSERT( !pImpl->pDdeService,
                 "Dde can not be initialized multiple times" );
 
